{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC re-verification on the committed tree `9906f0ec7b3`\n\nChecked ahead of the close so no criterion reaches the gate with its evidence\nunrecorded — the sibling story `fb5f-54fd-96cc-4105` failed its completion gate\non exactly that, with the work itself already correct.\n\n**AC1 — fixture records its SHA and re-derives exactly.** PASS.\n`python evals/similar-tickets/measure.py --check` → rc=0:\n\n```\nOK: 1524 pairs ({'lexical': 1431, 'semantic': 93}) over 630 tickets\nre-derive exactly at cad39ed1289\n```\n\nEvery pair id resolves in the store and the re-derived pair set matches the\nfixture exactly. The counts reproduce the plan's measured shape — 1,524 pairs,\n1,431 lexical, 93 semantic, 630 tickets — at tickets SHA `cad39ed1289`, which\nis the SHA the fixture header records (later than the `0b9294311b5` quoted in\nthe plan's Context, because the fixture was derived after that reading; the\ncriterion is internal consistency between header and re-derivation, and that\nholds).\n\n**AC2 — per-stratum recall@5 and recall@10 for all 3 candidates, no pooled\nfigure.** PASS. ADR 0122 lines 51–54 carry a table with separate semantic and\nlexical columns at both k values for `fts5`, `digest` and `vector`, plus a\n4th diagnostic `vector-raw` that the ADR explicitly labels as not one of the 3.\nThe exact command lines are quoted at lines 43–46. No pooled score appears;\nline 24 states the pooled figure is banned and why.\n\n**AC3 — one architecture named and justified from the semantic stratum, with\nthe operational record.** PASS. All required elements present:\n\n| element | where |\n|---|---|\n| chosen architecture | title: embed the LLM digest, surfaced at k=5 |\n| index path | `.rebar/cache/similar-tickets/` (line 138) |\n| freshness key | `reducer._cache.compute_dir_hash` (lines 142–146) |\n| catch-up rule | per-ticket dir-hash diff, incremental (lines 148–151) |\n| embedding model | `amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0` (3 mentions) |\n| per-ticket cost | 8 mentions |\n| bulk-duplicate artifact | lines 24–27 |\n\n**AC4 — ADR gates.** PASS. `scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` → rc=0;\n`scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` → rc=0.\n\n### Deviation from the plan, deliberate\n\nThe plan's Approach proposed the index at `<repo>/.git/rebar/similar.sqlite`,\nkeyed by tickets-branch HEAD SHA plus a format version. The ADR instead\nrecords `.rebar/cache/similar-tickets/`, keyed per ticket by the dir hash rebar\nalready computes to decide whether a ticket's reduced state changed.\n\nBoth satisfy AC3, which requires that an index path and freshness key be\nrecorded, not these particular ones. The substituted design is the stronger\none on the project's own terms: a branch-HEAD-plus-format-version key is a new\nfreshness mechanism that can drift from the store's notion of \"this ticket\nchanged\", and it invalidates the whole index on any write. The dir hash is\nthat notion, so it cannot drift, and it bounds work by write volume rather\nthan corpus size. It also introduces no new mechanism, which matters directly\nto the mechanism-delta ratchet.\n\nRecording it explicitly rather than letting the reviewer discover the\ndivergence between plan text and landed artifact.\n\n`make verify` is still running on this tree; its result will be recorded\nseparately.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793510616122622266,"uuid":"fa9575ff-312c-4d35-b59f-0c00db7fe761"}